1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,104
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,104 --> 00:00:07,836
Time to grade this morning's call — the part most shows skip.

3
00:00:07,836 --> 00:00:13,578
QUALCOMM, ticker QCOM never reached the trigger, so no position was taken.

4
00:00:13,578 --> 00:00:16,992
The entry did its quiet job: it kept us out.

5
00:00:16,992 --> 00:00:22,578
Chevron, ticker CVX never reached the trigger, so no position was taken.

6
00:00:22,578 --> 00:00:25,992
The entry did its quiet job: it kept us out.

7
00:00:25,992 --> 00:00:30,927
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

8
00:00:30,927 --> 00:00:36,336
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

9
00:00:36,301 --> 00:00:40,076
On the day, the book is up 492 dollars.

10
00:00:40,076 --> 00:00:43,368
Bruker (BRKR) leads, +7.3 percent.

11
00:00:43,368 --> 00:00:45,885
Deere & (DE) lags at -2.0.

12
00:00:45,885 --> 00:00:51,112
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

13
00:00:51,112 --> 00:00:53,739
Today's lesson is noise versus signal.

14
00:00:53,739 --> 00:00:57,404
Daily moves are weather; the weekly trend is climate.

15
00:00:57,404 --> 00:01:00,445
The system never exits on a scary afternoon.

16
00:01:00,445 --> 00:01:05,976
It acts only on weekly closes, because that is where the real information lives.

17
00:01:05,926 --> 00:01:13,133
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

18
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:21,413
12 positions, led by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing, ticker TSM, Avnet, ticker AVT, AbbVie, ticker ABBV.

19
00:01:21,413 --> 00:01:31,839
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

20
00:01:31,793 --> 00:01:36,675
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

21
00:01:36,675 --> 00:01:39,115
Every morning OROS proposes.

22
00:01:39,115 --> 00:01:49,837
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

23
00:01:49,837 --> 00:01:53,847
Inside the book today: 5 positions up, 7 down.

24
00:01:53,847 --> 00:01:56,288
Best, BRKR at +7.26 percent.

25
00:01:56,288 --> 00:01:57,944
Worst, DE at -2.05.

26
00:01:57,944 --> 00:02:03,000
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

27
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:10,235
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -3.00% per trade over 998 graded positions.

28
00:02:10,235 --> 00:02:17,383
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 50% position size.

29
00:02:17,383 --> 00:02:22,614
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

30
00:02:22,614 --> 00:02:35,166
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 183 names close the day in Stage 2; position size stays cut to 50% until the record earns it back.

31
00:02:35,137 --> 00:02:37,359
Over to the sports desk.

32
00:02:37,359 --> 00:02:46,526
Day 59 of the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

33
00:02:46,526 --> 00:02:51,340
In first place, the index fund, in gray, at 102,370.

34
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:58,192
Then the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, 1.7 thousand back at 100,694.

35
00:02:58,192 --> 00:03:05,322
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 4.8 thousand back at 97,598.

36
00:03:05,322 --> 00:03:07,914
The race has no finish line.

37
00:03:07,914 --> 00:03:12,173
Same books, same dollars, back at it tomorrow.

38
00:03:12,173 --> 00:03:16,988
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

39
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:18,840
Nothing is restated.

40
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:27,748
On screen, three equity lines grown from the same starting dollar: the frozen first book, the live book, and the index fund.

41
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:35,045
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

42
00:03:35,045 --> 00:03:37,286
Nothing here is financial advice.

43
00:03:37,286 --> 00:03:40,275
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
